 "_readme": "Country-level detail for the three compositions, applied by scripts/build_entities.py after the roll-ups. Each row names one country and one field. A row with 'groups' replaces the field with a census's own division of it and is always preferred; a row with only a 'note' says what a large residual holds and why it is not divided. Neither invents a split. This is the admin-0 counterpart of admin1_seed.json, and it is curated for the same reason: adapter output lands on admin1 and admin2 shapes, and the country record is the Factbook profile plus whatever its children roll up into it.",
